  "findings": [
    "Control and direct publication both allocate 40 VGPRs with a resource limit of 24 subgroups/SIMD. Direct has more static instructions but retains this allocation bucket.",
    "Local repair allocates 56 VGPRs versus 40 for direct, reducing the reported limit from 24 to 18. It may avoid expensive global replay but has a measured static resource cost.",
    "Full mip bounds allocate 48 VGPRs; gated and single-probe variants both allocate 64. One probe reduces lookup work without lowering the gated register-allocation bucket.",
    "No variant spills SGPRs/VGPRs or uses scratch. Shared adaptive fragment allocation remains 128 VGPRs / 8 subgroups throughout; instruction counts increase.",
    "V3 control retains 40 VGPRs but reports 2786 instructions / 14868 B versus 2783 / 14804 B in v2 after common native plane-time factoring. Flag-off semantics and image parity must be checked separately from binary identity."
  ]
